-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/34e9bd0f-f2a9-5432-985c-a529250ea061
-- title:
--   Descended chart and q+1 nodes at a supersingular place, q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q = 2$ (hypothesis `hq2`), $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and a rigidity guard is imposed: a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$.
--
--   *Reduction data.* $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, namely $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $\kappa = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$. $W$ is a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$ over $\kappa$ (this field is the $\kappa$-subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated by the $j$-expansion `jqModC` and its $M'$-fold $q$-expansion), and `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places, i.e. the places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}) \in \mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\kappa$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, the first being the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the full level-$M'$ modular function field $\mathbb{Q}(\mathrm{qExpand}\,d\,j : d \mid M')$, the second the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the $X_H$ function field at level $q^2M'$ with $H = \ker\big((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times\big)$. Next, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of the source, a surjective ring homomorphism $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal, whose restriction to constants is the residue map of $A$ and which matches $A$ on constants, together with a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisors of functions of nonzero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $s$ is one of the places in $W$.
--
--   *Small constants.* $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ has image in $A$; writing $A \cap k_0$ for $A.\mathrm{comap}$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the hypotheses require that $A \cap k_0$ be a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), henselian (`hhens`), with algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and that every $a \in A$ be congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0 \cap A$ (`hκ`). Further, $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; and $\varpi_t \in k_0$ has image in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   *Base layer.* $K_b$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$, $A_b$ is a valuation subring of $K_b$ consisting exactly of the elements whose image lies in $A$, and $\varpi_b \ne 0$ generates the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   *Conclusion.* Give $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ the $k_0$-algebra structure coming from $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Then for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $k_0$ which is characterised coefficientwise, in that $f \in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient $f_n$ ($n \in \mathbb{Z}$) lies in $k_0$, there exists a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with the following properties.
--
--   (1) $W_0$ meets constants correctly: for $x \in k_0$, the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ if and only if $x \in A$.
--
--   (2) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (3) The image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal.
--
--   (4) $W_0$ lies over $s$: for every $g$ in the full level-$M'$ modular function field over $\mathbb{Q}$ whose coefficientwise image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, which is regular wherever $j$ is (for every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of `jq` implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $g$), and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$: the image of $g$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ and $\mathrm{residue}_A(c) = s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}\,g)$, the difference (image of $g$) $-\, c$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal.
--
--   (5) Level stability: for every $\zeta$ in $\mathrm{Idx}\,q$ (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$), every $\gamma \in SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every $f \in F_0$ with $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,f \in F_0$, one has $f \in W_0$ if and only if $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,f \in W_0$.
--
--   (6) An affine chart: there exist a subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that:
--
--   (6a) the structure map sends $a \in A_b$ to the image of $a \in K_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$;
--
--   (6b) $B$ is contained in the compositum $k_0(\,\text{image of } K_b\,) \sqcup F_0$ inside $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$;
--
--   (6c) that compositum is the fraction field of $B$: every element of it is of the form $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$, $h \ne 0$;
--
--   (6d) $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$;
--
--   (6e) $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$;
--
--   (6f) every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$;
--
--   (6g) the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is prime;
--
--   (6h) $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ at that prime: $f \in F_0$ lies in $W_0$ if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $\varpi_b \nmid h$;
--
--   (6i) the image of `jq` in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ (through `hle`) lies in $B$;
--
--   (6j) $B$ is stable under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for all $\zeta$ and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$;
--
--   (6k) the special fibre is Drinfeld: for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$ for which the Drinfeld coordinate ring $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$ (the quotient of $\kappa[x_0,x_1]$ by $\mathrm{drinfeldPoly} - 1$) is a domain, and for every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ (the fixed field of the subgroup of the Drinfeld function field generated by the actions of $(1,\zeta')$, $\zeta' \in C_s$) such that: $\#C_s = \mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$; $\ker \rho$ is the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$; $\rho$ on constants is the residue map, $\rho(a) = \mathrm{residue}_A(a)$ for $a \in A_b$; $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ is the fraction field of the image, every $z$ being $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $\rho(h) \ne 0$; the image of $\rho$ consists exactly of those $z$ whose image in the Drinfeld function field lies in the image of $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$; and $\rho$ is equivariant, in that for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ in the subgroup $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ and $f \in B$ with $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1} f \in B$, the element $\rho(\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1} f)$ equals $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}\,q\,\kappa$ at $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ applied to $\rho(f)$, inside the Drinfeld function field;
--
--   (6l) nodes: there exists a finite set $\mathrm{nodes}$ of subrings of $F_0$ with $\#\mathrm{nodes} = q+1$ and:
--
--   — the level automorphisms permute the nodes: for all $\zeta$, all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and all $O \in \mathrm{nodes}$ there is $O' \in \mathrm{nodes}$ such that for $f \in F_0$ with $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,f \in F_0$, $f \in O$ if and only if $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,f \in O'$;
--
--   — the action is transitive: for all $\zeta$ and all $O, O' \in \mathrm{nodes}$ there is $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with, for $f \in F_0$ with $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,f \in F_0$, $f \in O$ if and only if $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,f \in O'$;
--
--   — distinct nodes are separated: for $O \ne O'$ in $\mathrm{nodes}$ there is $f \in F_0$ lying in both which is a non-unit of $O$ and a unit of $O'$;
--
--   — exhaustion: every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which meets constants as in (1) and satisfies the clause (4) with $V$ in place of $W_0$ either contains $B$ (every $f \in B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $V$), or dominates a node: there is $O \in \mathrm{nodes}$ with $O \subseteq V$ and every non-unit of $O$ in the maximal ideal of $V$;
--
--   — and for every $O \in \mathrm{nodes}$: $O \subseteq W_0$; $O$ is a local Noetherian ring; $O$ meets constants as in (1) (for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $O$); every $f \in O$ is congruent to a constant, i.e. there is $x \in k_0 \cap A$ with image in $O$ and $f - x$ a non-unit of $O$; and there are a natural number $E_0 \ge 1$, a unit $v$ of $A \cap k_0$ (both $v$ and $v^{-1}$ in $A$) with $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s}\,v$, a membership $\pi_0 \in O$, elements $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto the crossing model $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}$ over the adic completion $\widehat{A \cap k_0}$ with parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$ (that is, $\widehat{A\cap k_0}[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi_0^{E_0})$), and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that crossing model, such that: $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$ in $O$; $\iota$ sends the image of each $x \in k_0 \cap A$ to the constant $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel.const}$ of the image of $x$; $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U \cdot U$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V \cdot V$; $c_y$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal, while $c_x$, if it lies in $W_0$, is not in its maximal ideal; moreover
--
--   (i) there exists a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ containing $O$, meeting constants as in (1), which is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$, such that for some $t \in W_x$ and every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ then every coefficient of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$; such that $c_x$, if in $W_x$, lies in its maximal ideal, and $c_y$, if in $W_x$, does not; and such that for every $g$ in the full level-$M'$ modular function field with coefficientwise image in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and regular wherever $j$ is (as in (4)), the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_x$, lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ if and only if $R_0.\mathrm{residue}\,g = 0$, and, when $R_0.\mathrm{residue}\,g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, lies in $O$ and satisfies: for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ with image in $O$ and $\mathrm{residue}_A(c) = s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}\,g)$, the difference (image of $g$) $-\,c$ is a non-unit of $O$;
--
--   (ii) there exists a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ such that every element of $B_x$ lies in $B$ and in $O$; every element of $B_x$ is regular wherever the image of `jq` is, i.e. for every place $P$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of `jq` implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the element; $O$ is the localisation of $B_x$ at those elements of $B_x$ that are units of $O$, in the sense that $f \in O$ if and only if $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in B_x$ with $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h \in O$; $F_0$ is the fraction field of $B_x$, every $f \in F_0$ being of the form $g/h$ with $g,h \in B_x$, $h \ne 0$; and $B_x$ is finitely generated over the constants, namely $B_x$ is the subring generated by the images of the elements of $k_0 \cap A$ together with a finite set $T \subseteq F_0$.
--
--   This is the case $q = 2$, under the rigidity guard provided by an auxiliary prime $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the construction of the descended semistable model of the full-level modular curve at a supersingular place: over the level field $F_0$ of those functions whose $q$-expansion coefficients lie in the small field $k_0$, it produces the discrete valuation ring $W_0$ specialising to the supersingular place $s$, an $A_b$-affine chart $B$ whose special fibre is a quotient of the Drinfeld curve with level-equivariant parametrisation, and the $q+1$ nodes with their $\widehat{A\cap k_0}[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi_0^{E_0})$ crossing models. It is obtained by discarding clauses from [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_inertia_of_levelField_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_inertia_of_levelField_of_eq_two_of_dvd), and is in turn used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_drinfeldRing_iff_localization_formallySmooth_card_le_descent_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_drinfeldRing_iff_localization_formallySmooth_card_le_descent_of_eq_two_of_dvd) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_of_levelField_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_of_levelField_of_eq_two_of_dvd).
